------------------------- SSOutList: The next line(s) contains a list of output parameters that will be output in <rootname>.SD.out or <rootname>.out. ------
"M1N1TDxss, M1N1TDyss, M1N1TDzss"                               - Nodal translational displacements (TD) [m] at (0,0,0). Displacement results expressed in Substructure (SS) coordinate system (same as global). We don't request the rotations because SubDyn only provides the elastic part (not the rigid body motion part) since the development of large platform rotations.
"RBTDXss, RBTDYss, RBTDZss, RBRDXss, RBRDYss, RBRDZss"          - Rigid-body reference point translations [m] and rotations [rad]. The translations should be the same as "M1N1TDxss, M1N1TDyss, M1N1TDzss". The rotations should be better than "PtfmRoll, PtfmPitch, PtfmYaw" from ElastoDyn because the platform refence point is located at (0,0,0), but it comes from a rigid link from tower top. The tower is modeled in SubDyn.   
"M2N1FKxe, M2N1FKye, M2N1FKze, M2N1MKxe, M2N1MKye, M2N1MKze"    - Tower base loads: Fz [N], Fx [N], Fy [N], Mz [Nm], Mx [Nm], My [Nm]. Results from the spring element.
"M3N1FKxe, M3N1FKye, M3N1FKze, M3N1MKxe, M3N1MKye, M3N1MKze"    - Pontoon 3 (upwind) load cell loads at the pontoon root. xe in SubDyn corresponds to the longitudinal direction (from root to tip [proper sign]). ye in SubDyn corresponds to the vertical direction (upwards) [proper sign]. ze in SubDyn corresponds to the lateral direction (in +Y direction) [proper sign]. Equivalence from UMaine sensors: xp3 = -M2N1FKye, yp3 = M2N1FKze, zp3 = -M2N1FKxe.     
"M4N1FKxe, M4N1FKye, M4N1FKze, M4N1MKxe, M4N1MKye, M4N1MKze"    - Pontoon 3 (upwind) load cell loads at the pontoon outer position (results from beam). ze is the longitudinal diection. M4N1FKze is aligned with M3N1FKxe. ye is the vertical direction, but wrong sign. -M4N1FKye is aligned with M3N1FKye. xe is the lateral direction [proper sign]. M4N1FKxe is aligned with M3N1FKze. 
"M5N1FKxe, M5N1FKye, M5N1FKze, M5N1MKxe, M5N1MKye, M5N1MKze"    - Pontoon 1 (downwind -Y) load cell loads at the pontoon root. xe in SubDyn corresponds to the longitudinal direction (from root to tip ([proper sign]). ye in SubDyn corresponds to the vertical direction (upwards) [proper sign]. ze in SubDyn corresponds to the lateral direction (like -Y direction) [proper sign].  
"M6N1FKxe, M6N1FKye, M6N1FKze, M6N1MKxe, M6N1MKye, M6N1MKze"    - Pontoon 1 (downwind -Y) load cell loads at the pontoon outer position (results from beam). ze is the longitudinal diection. M6N1FKze is aligned with M5N1FKxe. ye is the vertical direction, but wrong sign. -M6N1FKye is aligned with M5N1FKye. xe is the lateral direction [proper sign]. M6N1FKxe is aligned with M5N1FKze. 
"M7N1FKxe, M7N1FKye, M7N1FKze, M7N1MKxe, M7N1MKye, M7N1MKze"    - Pontoon 2 (downwind +Y) load cell loads at the pontoon root. xe in SubDyn corresponds to the longitudinal direction (from root to tip [proper sign]). ye in SubDyn corresponds to the vertical direction (upwards) [proper sign]. ze in SubDyn corresponds to the lateral direction (like -Y direction) [proper sign].  
"M8N1FKxe, M8N1FKye, M8N1FKze, M8N1MKxe, M8N1MKye, M8N1MKze"    - Pontoon 2 (downwind +Y) load cell loads at the pontoon outer position (results from beam). The ze is the longitudinal diection. M8N1FKze is aligned with M7N1FKxe. ye is the vertical direction, but wrong sign. -M8N1FKye is aligned with M7N1FKye. xe is the lateral direction [proper sign]. M8N1FKxe is aligned with M7N1FKze.
END of output channels and end of file. (the word "END" must appear in the first 3 columns of this line)